ul: I'll create .git, commit base (exclude my 4 new files + S04-SHA256SUMS), add my files, run validate (no --no-diff), then remove .git entirely. Since this is all reversible and I verify path stays in workspace, it's safe.\n\nActually simpler and lower-risk: verify the ownership logic directly by replicating classifyChangedPathOwnership with my file list against my ownedPaths. But better to run the real thing.\n\nLet me do the git approach carefully."}}
